          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em K-orientation
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            (typically:
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_topological_ktheory In topological K-theory
          %h4#korientation_of_oriented_manifolds K-Orientation of oriented manifolds
          %p
            For ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            is K-oriented if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \oplus f^\ast(T Y)
            has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
          %p
            In this case there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+map"} Umkehr map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_! \colon K^\bullet(X) \to K^{\bullet + dim(Y) - dim(X)}(Y)
                  \\,.
          %h4#UniversalAtiyahBottShapiroOrientation The universal Atiyah-Bott-Shapiro orientation
          %p
            There is a universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+K-theory"} complex K-theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
                over
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structures"} spin^c structures
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
                over
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
          %p
            hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            homomorphisms out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin"} MSpin
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin"} MSpin
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⟶
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \longrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
          %p and
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin%5Ec"}
              MSpin
              %sup
                %i c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⟶
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \longrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
          %p
            These are (both) referred to as the
            %em Atiyah-Bott-Shapiro orientation
            (after
            = succeed ");" do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahBottShapiro64"} Atiyah-Bott-Shapiro 64
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Joachim04"} Joachim 04
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
            induced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo →
                  %mi KO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M Spin \to KO
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msup
                    %mi Spin
                    %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi KU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M Spin^c \to KU
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+genus"} Todd genus
          %p#OfCourse
            Of course,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU
            is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            and as such canonically comes with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy-commutative+ring+spectra"} homotopy-commutative ring spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                  %mo →
                  %mi KU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU \to KU
            (
            %a{:href => "complex+oriented+cohomology+theory#ComplexOrientationIsMUAlgebraStructure"}> this general Prop.
            , see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "spin%5Ec+structure#FromAlmostComplexStructures"} spin^c structure – from almost complex structure
          %p
            On this level there is also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+oriented+cohomology"} real orientation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+K-theory"} real K-theory
            given by a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi K
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M \mathbb{R} \longrightarrow K \mathbb{R}
          %p
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MR-theory"} MR-theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kriz01"}> Kriz 01, (3.20)
            ).
          %h4#ConnerFloydOrientation The universal Conner-Floyd orientation
          %p
            There are multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theories"} multiplicative cohomology theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy-commutative+ring+spectra"} homotopy-commutative ring spectra
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⟶
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \longrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
          %p and
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSU"} MSU
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⟶
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \longrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
          %p
            which are compatible in that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            formed by the evident vertical morphisms
