          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"}> commutes
            \.
          %p
            This
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+orientation"} Conner-Floyd orientation
            is originally due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"} Conner-Floyd 66, Section 5
          %p
            The morphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            reflects the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex orientation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            via the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+orientation+on+MU"} universal complex orientation on MU
          %h3#in_kktheory In KK-theory
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            %em K-orientation
            of this morphism is a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo !
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f! \in KK_d(B,A)
          %p
            such that (…). The corresponding
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gysin+map"} Gysin map
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            is then the postcomposition operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_! \colon K_\bullet(B) \simeq KK_\bullet(\mathbb{C}, B) \stackrel{f! \circ (-)}{\to} KK_\bullet(\mathbb{C}, A) \simeq K_{\bullet + d}(A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BMRS07"}> BMRS 07
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_the_relation_between_cobordisms_cohomology_and_ktheory As the relation between cobordisms cohomology and K-theory
          %p
            The Atiyah-Bott-Shapiro orientation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msup
                    %mi Spin
                    %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi KU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M Spin^c \to KU
            induces an equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo •
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo •
                        %mi c
                  %msub
                    %mi KU
                    %mo •
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi KU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M Spin^c_\bullet(-)\otimes_{M Spin^c_\bullet} KU_\bullet \simeq KU_\bullet(-)
          %p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo →
                  %mi KO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M Spin \to KO
            similarly induces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mi Spin
